# Byte-offset fixtures: the annotated-qmd example JSONs record byte offsets
# into these .qmd sources (and their line_breaks), so a CRLF checkout would
# shift every offset. Pin the whole directory, not just the .qmd sources: the
# JSON fixtures are single-line today, but the guard byte-compares them, so a
# future multi-line writer would break on Windows in exactly the way this pin
# exists to prevent (bd-1d6io).
ts-packages/annotated-qmd/examples/* text eol=lf
